# The tier images this repository builds ON, and the single place a bump happens.
#
# The image is three tiers, one published package each: an OS/toolchain base, the
# agent CLIs on top of it, and this repository on top of that. Only the last is
# rebuilt per commit — 25 MB against the 2167.8 MB a single-file build put on the
# wire — so the other two are named here by tag rather than built.
#
# BUMPING IS A DELIBERATE COMMIT, the same gesture as bumping GO_VERSION or
# CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION. The weekly base workflow publishes a new pair, runs the
# smoke suite against a candidate leaf, and prints the two lines to paste here
# when it is green. Nothing downstream moves until somebody pastes them.
#
# Both families are pinned because the slim Containerfiles are DERIVED (see
# ci-slim.sh) and a derived file cannot carry a pin of its own.
#
# These tags carry a BUILD timestamp, not a commit one: a base is rebuilt weekly
# whether or not anything was committed, so a commit-derived tag would name two
# different images and — GHCR tags being mutable — the second would silently
# overwrite the first.
AGENTS_REF=ghcr.io/codesweep-ai/sandbox-agents:v0.0.0-20260831030237-2b0141586e33
SLIM_AGENTS_REF=ghcr.io/codesweep-ai/sandbox-slim-agents:v0.0.0-20260831030237-2b0141586e33

